# px fixture: the copied FRAGMENT half of copy/paste. Rows: W20.
#
# Block text handed to the clipboard is verbatim: the attached comment, the
# nested body and the interior indent levels all come along. This file is that
# fragment as it sits on disk (tab-indented, one level deep, two top-level
# widgets so a multi-widget paste has a source too). Pasting it must strip the
# fragment's COMMON leading whitespace as a string prefix, convert interior
# indent LEVELS to the destination's unit, convert newlines to the
# destination's, and land by the same rules as an ordinary insert.

	# the A widget
	widget = {
		name = "px_fragment_a"
		icon = {
			size = { 4 4 }
		}
	}
	widget = {
		name = "px_fragment_b"
	}
